-- title:
--   Measurability of simultaneous approximate-fit failure
-- statement:
--   Let $d,n\ge0$ be integers, let $\Theta$ be a nonempty compact metric space with its Borel $\sigma$-algebra, and let $\theta:\Theta\to\mathbb R^d$ be continuous. Write $\varphi_d$ for the standard Gaussian density and, for a Borel probability measure $\mu$ on $\Theta$, put
--   $$
--   f_\mu(x)=\int_\Theta\varphi_d(x-\theta(a))\,d\mu(a),\qquad
--   \ell_w(x,\mu)=\sum_{i=1}^n w_i\log f_\mu(x_i).
--   $$
--   Here $x=(x_1,\ldots,x_n)$ is a data vector and $w\in\mathbb R^n$ is a weight vector. Let $\mathcal M_w(x)$ denote all maximizers of $\ell_w(x,\cdot)$ over probability measures on $\Theta$, and let $\mathbf1$ denote unit weights.
--
--   For two mixing laws $\nu,\mu_0$, define the ordinary likelihood gap and squared log-ratio discrepancy by
--   $$
--   D_x(\nu,\mu_0)=\ell_{\mathbf1}(x,\mu_0)-\ell_{\mathbf1}(x,\nu),\qquad
--   R_x(\nu,\mu_0)=\sum_{i=1}^n\left(\log\frac{f_\nu(x_i)}{f_{\mu_0}(x_i)}\right)^2.
--   $$
--
--   For arbitrary real numbers $\tau,t$, let $F_{\tau,t}$ consist of those $(x,w)$ for which some $\mu_w\in\mathcal M_w(x)$, $\mu_0\in\mathcal M_{\mathbf1}(x)$, and probability law $\nu$ satisfy
--   $$
--   \ell_w(x,\mu_w)-\tau\le\ell_w(x,\nu)
--   \quad\text{and}\quad
--   \bigl(D_x(\nu,\mu_0)>t\ \text{or}\ R_x(\nu,\mu_0)>t\bigr).
--   $$
--   Then $F_{\tau,t}$ is a Borel measurable subset of the data and weight space.
--
--   This identifies the failure of either uniform fit bound as a measurable event, so conditional bounds can later be integrated over the data.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/hanshengjiang/reweighted-npmle-lean/blob/5af8d16822c5a8a3f032b13eb95daea40f307484/ReweightedNPMLE/GaussianApproxJointEvents.lean#L49-L67

